    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "San Francisco covers the tip of a peninsula between the Pacific Ocean and San Francisco Bay. The city fits into about 120 square km, and more than 40 hills rise inside it, from Nob Hill to Twin Peaks.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The 1849 Gold Rush turned a settlement of about 1,000 people into a city of around 25,000 within a year. The 1906 earthquake and fire destroyed about 80 percent of it. Chinatown, founded in the 1850s, is the oldest in North America.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "September and October are the warmest months, when the summer fog lifts. Pack layers all year, as fog can drop the temperature fast from one neighbourhood to the next.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
